  "adaptationRules": [
    "A place.kind may be council, ward/division, state-district, federal-house-electorate, senate-region or another accurately named civic geography.",
    "Declare the actual entry routes, page choices, geometry layers, source fields and dates for the place. Keep statutory, statistical, electoral and cultural geographies distinct.",
    "Children and child maps are optional. Undivided councils and electorates do not acquire invented divisions. A missing or unpublished source is an explicit limitation.",
    "Counts, route names, timezone and identifiers below belong to this reviewed reference only. Replace them using that place's official evidence.",
    "The script is offline and read-only. It can detect structural regressions in declared scope; live links, law, geography, editorial care and interaction still need the listed human/browser checks.",
    "When an input bound to browser evidence changes, repeat the affected review, save its evidence, then deliberately replace that fingerprint. Do not auto-refresh review dates, hashes or passing results.",
    "Use declaredLayers/coverageNotes to disclose missing comparisons. An unbuilt state/federal overlay must not be described as an exact intersection analysis."
  ],
  "coverageNotes": [
    "Reference scope includes the Queensland council layer and ten Redland electoral divisions.",
    "Current state and federal electorates have source-map pathways; interactive state/federal overlay geometry and quantitative overlap analysis are not built in this reference.",
    "Individual candidate dossiers and a harvested voting-history database are not populated. Official pathways and ten dated councillor profile listings are present.",
    "The reference has no shared database, official submissions, currency issuance, candidate registration or election announcement."
